# Overall exposure ceiling for repro-daemon-worker.service, in tenths, PER
# HOST CLASS: `none = 26` means 2.6 on bare metal.
#
# The same unit, analysed by the same pinned binary, measures differently
# depending on whether the host is virtualised, because some of
# systemd-analyze's checks cannot be verified from inside a container or VM:
#
#   none         2.6  bare metal (gpu-server-001-mcl-bench-001, systemd 260.1,
#                     run 41208389754)
#   virtualized  3.1  ephemeral GARM runners (runs 41186521526, 41197758502,
#                     41201815981, 41251151966) -- 0.5 higher
#
# Recorded per class rather than routed to one class deliberately: both runner
# kinds register with the IDENTICAL labels `self-hosted,linux,x64`, so a job's
# `runs-on` cannot select the class a number was measured on. Giving the check
# the class is the only way to compare like with like.
#
# Neither number is a concession. Each is the measured value for its own class,
# so an exposure above its class's ceiling is a real regression, and a class
# with no line here is REFUSED rather than passed -- a new kind of runner has
# to be measured and recorded, never assumed.
none = 26
virtualized = 31
